BT /F1 11 Tf 50 780 Td 14 TL (IN THE COURT OF CIVIL JUDGE \(SR. DIV.\), SAKET COURTS, NEW DELHI) Tj T* (O.S. No. 245/2022 MEERA SHARMA v. ANIL VERMA) Tj T* () Tj T* (PLAINT) Tj T* (SUIT FOR SPECIFIC PERFORMANCE OF AGREEMENT TO SELL AND PERMANENT INJUNCTION) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. That the plaintiff Meera Sharma is a resident of Saket, New Delhi. The defendant) Tj T* (Anil Verma is the owner of Flat No. B-204, Sunrise Apartments, Saket, New Delhi \(the) Tj T* (suit property\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (2. That on 10.01.2022 the defendant agreed in writing to sell the suit property to the) Tj T* (plaintiff for a total sale consideration of Rs. 64,00,000 under an Agreement to Sell) Tj T* (executed at Saket, New Delhi.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3. That on 10.01.2022 the plaintiff paid Rs. 8,00,000 in cash to the defendant as) Tj T* (advance towards the sale consideration, in the presence of Deepak Arora, and the) Tj T* (defendant acknowledged receipt of the amount in the Agreement to Sell.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4. That the balance of Rs. 56,00,000 was payable at the time of registration of the) Tj T* (sale deed on or before 05.02.2022.) Tj T* () Tj T* (5. That the plaintiff has always been ready and willing to perform her part of the) Tj T* (agreement, but the defendant has failed and refused to execute the sale deed and has) Tj T* (threatened to sell the suit property to a third party.) Tj T* () Tj T* (6. That the plaintiff therefore prays for a decree of specific performance directing) Tj T* (the defendant to execute the sale deed, and for a permanent injunction restraining the) Tj T* (defendant from selling or parting with possession of the suit property.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Plaintiff, through Adv. Rohan Kapoor. Filed on 14.02.2022.) Tj T* ET
